Theorem TF-5: Apply (no contract) transfer produces CONSERVATIVE

  Preconditions:
    - Instruction is `Apply { dst, func, args }` per Annex E §AIMS TF-5
    - `func` has NO `MemoryContract` available (unknown callee — direct call
      to unresolved fn, dyn-trait dispatch lacking contract, opaque FFI)
    - CONSERVATIVE per Annex E §AIMS TF-5 + Appendix A row 6:
      `(Owned, Unrestricted, Many, MaybeShared, Unknown, NonReusable, ALL)`
      where ALL = 0b111 = {may_alloc=true, may_share=true, may_throw=true}

  Soundness property:
    transfer_tf5(Apply { _, _, _ }) = CONSERVATIVE (constant function,
    independent of input state and arg values).
    L-6 layer (b) monotonicity: f(_) = CONSERVATIVE is constant; trivially
    monotone per L-4 reflexivity.

  Proof obligation:
    Three-part discharge:
      (a) Output enumeration — verify Appendix A row 6 emission column-wise:
          access = Owned; consumption = Unrestricted; cardinality = Many;
          uniqueness = MaybeShared; locality = Unknown;
          shape = NonReusable; effect = ALL = 0b111.
      (b) CONSERVATIVE design correctness check — verify the value is
          operationally correct, NOT lattice TOP per Annex E §AIMS TF-5:
          "MaybeShared NOT Shared — enables dynamic COW. CONSERVATIVE NOT
          lattice TOP for Uniqueness." Shared would be TOP for Uniqueness
          (Unique ≤ MaybeShared ≤ Shared); CONSERVATIVE picks MaybeShared
          to enable runtime IsShared (DP-4) check vs forcing static copy.
      (c) L-6 layer (b) monotonicity — constant function f(_) = CONSERVATIVE
          trivially monotone: forall a, b in AimsState input domain,
          f(a) = f(b) = CONSERVATIVE; CONSERVATIVE ≤ CONSERVATIVE by L-4
          reflexivity; hence f(a) ≤ f(b).

    Part (a) — column-wise verification:
      Access = Owned: Apply result is owned by the caller (callee returned
        a fresh reference, OR transferred ownership of a callee-local).
      Consumption = Unrestricted: caller may use the result arbitrarily.
      Cardinality = Many: backward analysis refines actual usage; forward
        emits the most-permissive value.
      Uniqueness = MaybeShared: NOT Shared — preserves the runtime
        IsShared check option for dynamic COW (RL-7).
      Locality = Unknown: unknown callee may return any locality.
      Shape = NonReusable: no shape information available without contract.
      Effect = ALL: unknown callee may allocate / share / throw.

    Part (b) — non-TOP-for-Uniqueness check per §3 TF-5 explicit guidance:
      Verifier ensures CONSERVATIVE.uniqueness != Shared.
      Per UNIQUENESS_CARRIER chain {Unique, MaybeShared, Shared}, Shared is
      the chain's top element. CONSERVATIVE picks MaybeShared — a deliberate
      design choice to preserve dynamic-COW eligibility (DP-4 returns true
      on MaybeShared, false on Shared). Engine verifies this invariant by
      asserting CONSERVATIVE.uniqueness == "MaybeShared" — not "Shared".

    Part (c) — constant-function monotonicity:
      f(_) = CONSERVATIVE = (Owned, Unrestricted, Many, MaybeShared, Unknown,
      NonReusable, 0b111). For any state pair (a, b) with a ≤ b in the
      input domain, f(a) = f(b) = CONSERVATIVE. By L-4 reflexivity,
      CONSERVATIVE ≤ CONSERVATIVE on the product lattice (every dimension
      reflexively comparable). Hence f(a) ≤ f(b).

    Engines dispatched:
      monotonicity (PRIMARY — L-6 layer (b) constant-function discharge per
        section_04::verify_tf5_apply_no_contract_conservative)
      case_analysis (PRIMARY — Appendix A row 6 forward-transfer column
        verification + non-TOP design-correctness check per
        section_04::verify_tf5_apply_no_contract_conservative)
      lattice (SECONDARY — accepts gracefully)
      refinement (SECONDARY — accepts gracefully; TF-5 emits CONSERVATIVE
        directly; refine() is TF-6 / TF-6a territory)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_04 monotonicity + case_analysis engines discharge TF-5 via Appendix A row 6 column-wise emission + non-TOP-for-Uniqueness design check + constant-function monotonicity
